<title>USA: Maine turnpike hears mixed views on expansion.</title>
<headline>Maine turnpike hears mixed views on expansion.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Maine Turnpike Authority heard mixed testimony on whether the southern portion of the 99-mile toll road should be widened.</p>
<p>Some regular commuters said the road was too congested and that the Authority should increase the number of lanes from four to six.</p>
<p>But several environmental groups argue the heavy congestion is limited to just 19 hours a year, and that does not warrant spending more than $100 million dollars.</p>
<p>((Joan Gralla, 212-859-1654))</p>
</text>
